LATEST IMPLEMENTATION — MB-02C
mirror_chain::v2 provides NetworkManifestV2, ManifestIdentityV2, ChainV2,
ChainReplayExpectationV2, genesis_template_v2 and typed errors. The chain owns a
private exact manifest, accepted full blocks, combined ledger and resource counters.
Acceptance has no arbitrary ledger/cache installation or external ancestry argument.
The lower-level bind_to_validated_block still only attaches trusted provenance;
ChainV2 establishes that provenance through its own actual block validation.

MNM2 is public metadata, not a biometric archive or master credential. Exact order:
magic[4]=MNM2, version:u16=2, config_length:u32, exact MCF2, proof_count:u32,
ordered 64-byte seed signatures, exact genesis_hash[32]. Integers are little-endian;
hashes are raw bytes. Size is 46 + config_length + 64 * proof_count. Maximum MCF2
is 2,717,590 bytes; maximum proofs 1,000; maximum MNM2 is 2,781,636 bytes.
Proof count equals bootstrap count and EVERY ordered proof verifies under C.
new(config, proofs, pin) explicitly selects the network. decode_for(bytes, identity)
requires independently chosen C/genesis, preflights complete framing before
allocation/signature work, and rejects unknown versions, trailing/oversized data
and invalid proofs. Do not derive trusted expectations from the peer/input they check.

Genesis requires V2, exact C, height zero, zero parent, empty operations with their
correct root, executed verified-bootstrap ledger root, exact configured timestamp/
bits and valid work. The actual hash must equal the manifest pin; another valid
nonce is a different genesis. A deliberately pinned malformed genesis must still
pass every field/root check. genesis_template_v2 produces an unaccepted nonce-zero
proposal; mining and acceptance remain separate steps.

mirror_consensus::v2 requires literal configured pow_bits, then the existing compact
semantics over big_endian_integer(SHA256d("MIRROR_BLOCK_V2" || header160)) <= target.
No digest reversal. A compact alias with the same numeric target still fails literal
bits equality. Existing accepted positive noncanonical configured targets remain
supported. No retargeting. mine_header_v2 includes the initial nonce and changes
only nonce, with explicit local budget 1..=1,000,000. A solution on the last allowed
attempt or at u64::MAX succeeds; a failed maximum nonce never wraps. MineResultV2
is not an acceptance certificate. Easy work is not encryption, equal-human consensus
or reward assignment.

CHILD ACCEPTANCE ORDER
1. Full body/count/size and cumulative branch budgets before expensive state work.
2. Version/C, checked next height, actual parent hash, strict child timestamp > parent.
3. Exact configured bits and actual work.
4. Exact ordered full signed-operation commitment.
5. LedgerV2::stage_operations on the COMPLETE ORIGINAL body, using this chain's
   immutable accepted prefix as ParentChainViewV2. Signatures, context and state
   execute in original order; no signature prepass masks an earlier execution error.
6. Compare the computed combined ledger root with the claimed header root.
7. Reserve the block slot, bind its actual hash and install block/ledger/counters.
Every returned error preserves the whole accepted ChainV2. prepare_candidate is
read-only and unaccepted; append still revalidates after mining. Empty blocks process
expiry, height and ledger root. Timestamps have no wall-clock/future ceiling;
accepted u64::MAX has no successor. This synthetic rule is not production liveness.
Standard infallible allocations can still terminate a process; this is not crash safety.

FULL REPLAY AND RESOURCE CONTRACT
ChainV2::replay and replay_encoded require an external Copy expectation containing
C, genesis_hash, height, tip_hash and ledger_root. Aggregate input count/bytes are
preflighted before input-sized cloning/decoding. Every actual block validates from
genesis through the same append path, then final tip/root compare. Wrong intermediate
roots, old valid prefixes and foreign anchors reject without returning a partial
chain. checkpoint() reads accepted state; it does not discover global latestness.
Competing branches can both validate. This slice supplies no canonical fork choice,
finality, durable publication, network transport or V2 node daemon.

Inclusive caps: 4,096 blocks INCLUDING genesis, 16 MiB canonical MRB2 history, and
1,048,576 cumulative abstract state/configuration items. Genesis charge is twice
the configured seed-plus-allocation entry count. Each child charges configuration
entries + current account count + current membership record count + retained approval
count + one per incoming Transfer/Enroll/Approve. Withdraw adds no incoming item.
Charges are checked before staging and committed only on success. This is abstract
work accounting, not measured CPU, exact allocations or a population limit.
No eviction, pruning, automatic cap increase or partial replay success. At exhaustion
this finite component stops growing. Future changes require reviewed profile/version
semantics. Preserve these bounds in storage/recovery too.

